menu "Michi Music Stream Button"

    comment "Deterministic gestures (contract in michi_button_gesture.h): short press (< RECOVERY_PRESS_MS) opens the pairing window; long press (>= RECOVERY_PRESS_MS and < FACTORY_RESET_PRESS_MS) runs recovery ONLY in RECOVERABLE_ERROR; very long press (>= FACTORY_RESET_PRESS_MS) runs the factory reset (armed). Both gestures are ALWAYS available - no choice can build a firmware without the physical factory reset."

    config MICHI_BUTTON_DEBOUNCE_MS
        int "Debounce window (ms)"
        default 20
        range 10 200
        help
          Stable-window debounce: an edge (press/release) is confirmed only
          after N consecutive equal samples, N = DEBOUNCE/POLL rounded up.
          The stable window is (N-1) poll periods; POLL must be < DEBOUNCE
          or the debounce is disabled (init clamps N to 2 and logs a
          warning). Honest guarantee: glitches shorter than one poll period
          are rejected (they cannot fill N consecutive samples); a bounce
          longer than the poll period can confirm an edge if it spans the
          whole stable window - contacts that bounce long need a larger
          window.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_RECOVERY_PRESS_MS
        int "Recovery press threshold (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 500 30000
        help
          Press duration (measured edge-to-edge from the ISR timestamps) at
          or above which the press counts as LONG and runs the RECOVERY
          gesture (post MICHI_EVENT_RECOVER) instead of pairing. Recovery
          fires only when the FSM is in RECOVERABLE_ERROR at the release;
          in any other state the long press is ignored. 5 s is long enough
          that a normal pairing tap can never trip it. Must be <
          MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_RESET_PRESS_MS (the factory-reset range is
          bounded by this symbol; a build-time assert backs it up).

    config MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_RESET_PRESS_MS
        int "Factory reset press threshold (ms)"
        default 10000
        range MICHI_BUTTON_RECOVERY_PRESS_MS 60000
        help
          Press duration at or above which the press runs the FACTORY
          RESET gesture (wipe the whole NVS partition - identity,
          controllers, wifi credentials, DAC override, server_id - and
          restart) instead of recovery/pairing. 10 s is deliberately
          distinct from the 5 s recovery gesture so a recovery hold can
          never drift into a destructive reset. Always available in the
          default build (no choice): a corrupt identity store has no
          other physical recovery path.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_FACTORY_ARM_MS
        int "Factory reset arm window (ms)"
        default 10000
        range 0 300000
        help
          A factory reset runs only if the press STARTED at least this many
          milliseconds after boot (measured with esp_timer_get_time()
          against the button init reference). A button held through
          power-on, or a stuck pin, would otherwise confirm a "press" with
          ~0 ms elapsed as soon as the FSM leaves the protected states and
          erase NVS. 0 disables the arm window. Recovery is NOT gated by
          the arm window (a recoverable error right after boot must stay
          recoverable).

    config MICHI_BUTTON_POLL_MS
        int "Debounce task poll period (ms)"
        default 10
        range 1 50
        help
          Sampling period of the debounce task. 10 ms gives sub-tick
          resolution for the press duration while keeping the task at 100
          samples/s of a single GPIO read. Must be < MICHI_BUTTON_DEBOUNCE_MS:
          POLL >= DEBOUNCE disables the debounce (N would be 1; init clamps
          N to 2 and logs a warning).

    config MICHI_BUTTON_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Debounce task stack (bytes)"
        default 3072
        range 2048 16384
        help
          Stack of the debounce task (ESP-IDF xTaskCreate takes bytes).
          The task polls one GPIO and posts events, so the default is
          generous.

endmenu
